### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Subscribe — channel_created. NOT scopable at all — no `config` accepted (GET /triggers above shows
### `config: null` for it) since the channel this event reports doesn't exist until the event fires. Always
### workspace-wide.
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/triggers/slack/channel_created/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{slack_connection_id}}",
  "webhook_url": "https://webhook.site/your-unique-url-here",
  "extra_metadata": { "notes": "for the #support-eu channel" }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Subscribe — file_shared, scoped to one channel. Needs the files:read bot EVENT scope (distinct from
### files:write, which upload_file the ACTION uses) — see .env.example. Slack's file_shared event only
### carries IDs (file_id/channel_id/user_id), not the filename/title — call files.info with file_id if you
### need those (no files.info action exists in this app yet).
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/triggers/slack/file_shared/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{slack_connection_id}}",
  "webhook_url": "https://webhook.site/your-unique-url-here",
  "config": { "channel_id": "{{slack_channel}}" },
  "extra_metadata": { "notes": "for the #support-eu channel" }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Bad config shape — 400s with a real zod issue naming the trigger, not a silent no-op (channel_id must
### be a string; trigger_routes.ts validates `config` against THIS trigger's own schema once it knows
### which trigger this is, not against a generic z.unknown() at the body-parse stage). Note this is a
### DIFFERENT failure mode than passing a well-typed but wrong value (e.g. a "#name" instead of a real
### ID) — that's still a valid string, so it parses fine here and just silently never matches any event
### instead (matchesConfig does a plain equality check, no Slack API call to reject it with an error).
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/triggers/slack/new_message/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{slack_connection_id}}",
  "webhook_url": "https://webhook.site/your-unique-url-here",
  "config": { "channel_id": 12345 },
  "extra_metadata": { "notes": "for the #support-eu channel" }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Slack's own Events API delivery endpoint — this is what Slack calls, not something a client calls
### directly. Included here for reference/local testing (e.g. replaying a captured payload with curl).
### First-time setup: Slack sends a `url_verification` challenge here and expects it echoed back.
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/webhooks/slack/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "url_verification",
  "challenge": "test-challenge-token"
}

# ============================================================================
# ADMIN — read-only inspection, filter by app in the response yourself (no per-app query param)
# ============================================================================

### 🔧 Admin — users
GET {{base_url}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}

### 🔧 Admin — trigger instances
GET {{base_url}}/admin/triggers
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}

### 🔧 Admin — action/trigger call log
GET {{base_url}}/admin/logs?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}
